 "content": "A Promotion"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le01ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to spill "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to allow a liquid to leave a container without intention"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I feel really bad I spilled coffee on your assistant."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le01ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use at work."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "assistant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who helps another person in an office"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Is your assistant angry that I spilled coffee?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le01ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "efficient"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "works quickly and accurately"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You are an efficient worker."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le01ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "educational outreach"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "communications designed to train or teach the public"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will be responsible for educational outreach."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le01ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "blog"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an electronic journal "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You'll write blogs and articles for the company website. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le01ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "focus group"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a meeting organized by a business to understand people's opinions"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You'll also plan focus group sessions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le01ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.<br/> Regular verbs end in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"strong\">-ied</span>.<br/> Irregular verbs change in different ways.<br/> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">did</span> followed by the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask ... ?</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"italic\">to do</span>."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to spill \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spilled\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to copy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"copied\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to protect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"protected\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to lose\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"lost\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was, were\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to speak \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spoke\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to think\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thought\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I had problems last week. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I didn't finish the report on time."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future tense to talk actions in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">will</span> goes before the verb. The short form is <span class=\"strong\">'ll.</span><br/><br/>You use the Future tense when you talk about intentions, make offers or make predictions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will finish the project soon. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You will be responsible for educational outreach."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We'll send the invitations."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Listen to the songs \"I Will Always Love You\" by Whitney Houston and \"I Will Survive\" by Gloria Gaynor online."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Print and read the lyrics of each song."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Underline the examples of the Future tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, discuss which song you prefer and explain why."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I listen to two English songs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I listen for sentences about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss the songs with a partner."}]}], "type": "sena"}